    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess i see what you mean about being free. no more expectations, no more needing to be \"on\" for anyone. but that freedom feels so heavy when there's nothing left to do. once you've done everything you were meant to do... does the silence ever just feel like a natural place to stop? like, if the story is done, why keep dragging out the epilogue?",
